  {
    "id": "ig_ucr_trc_p3997977884484909767",
    "title": "2026 Tomas Rivera Conference",
    "description": "Before it hit the big screen in 1981, \"Zoot Suit\" made history as the very first Chicano play produced on Broadway.\n\nWritten and directed by Luis Valdez, this revolutionary work brought the energy, style, and resilience of the 1940s Pachuco culture front and center. \n\nLearn about the legacy of this groundbreaking writer and director at UCR on Oct. 15 at the 2026 Tomas Rivera Conference.\n\ntomasriveraconference.ucr.edu\n\n#ZootSuit #LuisValdez #ChicanoTheater #ChicanoFilm #BroadwayHistory #UCRiverside #UCRCHASS #TomasRiveraConference\n\n\"Zoot Suit\" poster from IMDB",
    "starts_at": "2026-10-15T07:00:00+00:00",
    "ends_at": "2026-10-16T07:00:00+00:00",
    "location": "UCR",
